# Scacelith - Polski
# Translation of assets/i18n/en.lang (same keys, same {n}). Plurals have three forms:
# one (1)|few (2-4, 22-24, 32-34...)|many (0, 5-21, 25-31...).
# Register: informal "ty", as Polish system software uses. Buttons and commands in the imperative
# ("Zapisz", "Cofnij ruch"), status messages impersonal or as nouns ("Zapisano partię").
# The player's and the opponent's gender is unknown: no second-person past tense, no adjective or
# participle agreeing with a person; present tense, impersonal forms or nouns instead.
# Terms follow the Polish glossary (partia, bierka, sędzia, tempo gry, blankiet, remis na żądanie).
# Titles are written in capitals (the title face is an inscriptional capital face).

